NAME
    stat - show a file's metadata

SYNOPSIS
    stat PATH

DESCRIPTION
    Print what the filesystem says about PATH: its type, its mode both
    symbolically and in octal, its owner (name, uid and gid), its size,
    its link count and its inode number.

    The mode is the truth about who may do what: the owner bits are your
    session's rights, the other bits a bound on everyone else's grants
    (fs.policy(5)). The owner is your session's account. Nothing about
    either is stored on the disk.

SEE ALSO
    chmod(1), chown(8), ls(1), ln(1)
